ss\",\n      \"Recording attendance\",\n      \"Rewarding effort\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Identifying learning needs and progress\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Ranking can demotivate and doesn't guide instruction effectively.\",\n      \"Correct! Assessment diagnoses strengths and needs, guiding targeted instruction and measuring growth.\",\n      \"Attendance tracking is administrative, not instructional assessment.\",\n      \"While recognition matters, assessment's primary purpose is diagnostic and instructional.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q124\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which element defines fluent reading?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Slow, careful decoding\",\n      \"Smooth, accurate, expressive reading\",\n      \"Memorization of every word\",\n      \"Reading silently only\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Smooth, accurate, expressive reading\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Slow, careful reading indicates developing fluency, not fluent reading.\",\n      \"Correct! Fluent reading is smooth, accurate, and expressive with appropriate pacing and prosody.\",\n      \"Fluency involves automatic decoding, not memorization of all words.\",\n      \"Fluency applies to both oral and silent reading.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q125\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which best defines language register?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Vocabulary level only\",\n      \"Sentence structure\",\n      \"Level of formality for audience and purpose\",\n      \"Tone of voice\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Level of formality for audience and purpose\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Register involves more than just vocabulary—it includes style and formality across all language elements.\",\n      \"Sentence structure is one component but doesn't fully define register.\",\n      \"Correct! Language register is the degree of formality adjusted for specific contexts, audiences, and purposes.\",\n      \"Tone is related but distinct from register; register encompasses broader stylistic choices.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q126\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"What does code-switching demonstrate?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Poor grammar use\",\n      \"Flexibility in language based on audience\",\n      \"Avoidance of cultural norms\",\n      \"Memorization of word roots\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Flexibility in language based on audience\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Code-switching is a sophisticated linguistic skill, not poor grammar.\",\n      \"Correct! Code-switching shows linguistic flexibility and cultural awareness by adapting language to different situations and audiences.\",\n      \"Code-switching actually demonstrates awareness and respect for cultural norms.\",\n      \"Word roots relate to morphology, not code-switching.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q127\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Hard\",\n    \"question\": \"What branch of linguistics studies meaning in context?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Phonology\",\n      \"Morphology\",\n      \"Pragmatics\",\n      \"Semantics\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Pragmatics\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Phonology studies sound systems in language.\",\n      \"Morphology examines word structure and formation.\",\n      \"Correct! Pragmatics analyzes how context, speaker intent, and social factors influence meaning.\",\n      \"Semantics studies meaning but doesn't emphasize context as pragmatics does.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q128\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which sentence shows positive connotation?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"He's cheap.\",\n      \"He's thrifty.\",\n      \"He's stingy.\",\n      \"He's miserly.\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"He's thrifty.\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"'Cheap' has negative connotations of low quality or excessive frugality.\",\n      \"Correct! 'Thrifty' has positive connotations of wise money management.\",\n      \"'Stingy' has negative connotations of unwillingness to spend or share.\",\n      \"'Miserly' has strongly negative connotations of excessive hoarding.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q129\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Denotation refers to a word's…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Historical origin\",\n      \"Literal meaning\",\n      \"Figurative association\",\n      \"Emotional tone\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Literal meaning\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Etymology studies historical origins, not denotation.\",\n      \"Correct! Denotation is the dictionary definition or literal meaning of a word.\",\n      \"Figurative associations relate to connotation, not denotation.\",\n      \"Emotional tone is part of connotation, not denotation.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q130\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which is NOT a key component of communication?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Sender\",\n      \"Message\",\n      \"Grammar\",\n      \"Feedback\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Grammar\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"The sender initiates communication.\",\n      \"The message is the content being communicated.\",\n      \"Correct! While grammar aids clarity, it's not one of the six essential components of the communication process.\",\n      \"Feedback allows the sender to gauge message reception.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q131\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which quality ensures effective communication?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Ambiguity\",\n      \"Clarity\",\n      \"Volume\",\n      \"Length\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Clarity\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Ambiguity obscures meaning and hinders communication.\",\n      \"Correct! Clarity ensures the message is understood as intended.\",\n      \"Volume is a delivery factor but doesn't guarantee effective communication.\",\n      \"Length doesn't ensure effectiveness; conciseness is often preferable.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q132\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Tone is defined as…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The emotional quality or attitude in language\",\n      \"The complexity of sentence structure\",\n      \"The literal meaning of a word\",\n      \"The rhythm of speech\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"The emotional quality or attitude in language\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Tone reflects the speaker's or writer's attitude toward the subject and audience.\",\n      \"Sentence complexity relates to syntax, not tone.\",\n      \"Literal meaning is denotation, not tone.\",\n      \"Rhythm relates to prosody, not tone (though they can work together).\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q133\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Active listening means…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Hearing and ignoring irrelevant details\",\n      \"Responding thoughtfully and showing understanding\",\n      \"Taking notes only\",\n      \"Finishing sentences for the speaker\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Responding thoughtfully and showing understanding\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Active listening requires engagement with all content, not selective ignoring.\",\n      \"Correct! Active listening involves full attention, comprehension, and meaningful response.\",\n      \"Note-taking is one strategy but doesn't encompass active listening.\",\n      \"Interrupting shows poor listening, not active engagement.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q134\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Nonverbal cues can…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Only distract from meaning\",\n      \"Reinforce or contradict verbal messages\",\n      \"Replace written communication\",\n      \"Eliminate misunderstanding entirely\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Reinforce or contradict verbal messages\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Nonverbal cues enhance and clarify, not just distract.\",\n      \"Correct! Nonverbal communication can support, emphasize, or contradict spoken words.\",\n      \"Written communication serves different purposes; nonverbal cues complement but don't replace it.\",\n      \"While helpful, nonverbal cues alone can't eliminate all misunderstanding.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q135\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Hard\",\n    \"question\": \"Which is an example of situational irony?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The reader knows the killer's identity before the detective does.\",\n      \"A fire station burns down.\",\n      \"A repeated vowel sound in poetry.\",\n      \"The moral lesson of a story.\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"A fire station burns down.\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"This is dramatic irony, where the audience knows more than the characters.\",\n      \"Correct! Situational irony occurs when the outcome contradicts expectations—a fire station should prevent fires, not burn.\",\n      \"This describes assonance, a sound device, not irony.\",\n      \"This describes theme or moral, not irony.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q136\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Symbolism adds meaning by…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Simplifying description\",\n      \"Representing abstract ideas through concrete objects\",\n      \"Listing adjectives\",\n      \"Creating suspense\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Representing abstract ideas through concrete objects\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Symbolism adds complexity, not simplification.\",\n      \"Correct! Symbols use tangible objects to represent abstract concepts, adding layers of meaning.\",\n      \"Listing adjectives is descriptive technique, not symbolism.\",\n      \"While symbols can contribute to atmosphere, their primary function is representing deeper meaning.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q137\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"A third-person limited narrator…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Knows all characters' thoughts\",\n      \"Only knows one character's perspective\",\n      \"Uses 'you' to address the reader\",\n      \"Is part of the story's action\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Only knows one character's perspective\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Knowing all characters' thoughts describes third-person omniscient.\",\n      \"Correct! Third-person limited provides insight into one character's mind while maintaining narrative distance.\",\n      \"Using 'you' describes second-person point of view.\",\n      \"Being part of the action describes first-person narration.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q138\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Conflict in a story is…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The climax\",\n      \"The struggle between opposing forces\",\n      \"The exposition\",\n      \"The resolution\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"The struggle between opposing forces\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"The climax is the turning point, not the conflict itself.\",\n      \"Correct! Conflict is the central struggle driving the plot, whether internal or external.\",\n      \"Exposition provides background information.\",\n      \"Resolution shows how the conflict is settled.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q139\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Theme is best described as…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The moral lesson or universal truth of the story\",\n      \"The plot's main event\",\n      \"The story's timeline\",\n      \"The setting's location\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"The moral lesson or universal truth of the story\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Theme is the underlying message or insight about life that the work explores.\",\n      \"The main event is part of plot, not theme.\",\n      \"Timeline relates to plot structure.\",\n      \"Location is an element of setting, not theme.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q140\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Diction refers to…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Sentence structure\",\n      \"Word choice\",\n      \"Figurative meaning\",\n      \"Dialogue pacing\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Word choice\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Sentence structure is syntax, not diction.\",\n      \"Correct! Diction is the writer's selection and use of specific words to create meaning and tone.\",\n      \"Figurative meaning involves literary devices like metaphor.\",\n      \"Dialogue pacing relates to narrative structure.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q141\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which sentence best shows imagery?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"He walked slowly.\",\n      \"The sunlight spilled like honey across the table.\",\n      \"She moved quickly.\",\n      \"It was late.\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"The sunlight spilled like honey across the table.\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"This is simple description without sensory detail.\",\n      \"Correct! This creates vivid sensory experience through visual and metaphorical language.\",\n      \"This states action without engaging the senses.\",\n      \"This provides information without sensory detail.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q142\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"An author's voice reflects…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The plot's complexity\",\n      \"The writer's individual style and tone\",\n      \"The story's setting\",\n      \"The genre of the work\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"The writer's individual style and tone\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Plot complexity is a structural choice, not voice.\",\n      \"Correct! Voice is the distinctive personality and perspective that comes through the author's stylistic choices.\",\n      \"Setting is a story element, not voice.\",\n      \"Genre is a category; voice is individual to the writer.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q143\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Hard\",\n    \"question\": \"Syntax primarily affects…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Sentence rhythm and emphasis\",\n      \"Theme development\",\n      \"Characterization\",\n      \"Symbolism\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Sentence rhythm and emphasis\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Syntax—the arrangement of words and phrases—shapes how sentences flow and what gets emphasized.\",\n      \"Theme emerges from content and meaning, not sentence structure.\",\n      \"Characterization involves personality development, not syntax.\",\n      \"Symbolism uses objects for meaning, unrelated to syntax.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q144\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-3\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Tone in writing reveals…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The author's attitude\",\n      \"The story's location\",\n      \"The text's theme\",\n      \"The rhythm of language\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"The author's attitude\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Tone conveys the author's attitude toward the subject and audience through stylistic choices.\",\n      \"Location is setting, not tone.\",\n      \"Theme is the underlying message; tone is how it's expressed.\",\n      \"Rhythm relates to syntax and sound patterns.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q145\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which best defines theme?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Setting of the story\",\n      \"Sequence of events\",\n      \"Central message or universal idea\",\n      \"Character's motivation\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Central message or universal idea\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Setting provides the time and place, not the theme.\",\n      \"Sequence of events describes plot, not theme.\",\n      \"Correct! Theme is the underlying message or universal truth explored in the work.\",\n      \"Motivation drives character actions but isn't the theme.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q146\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Characterization is developed through…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Dialogue, actions, and description\",\n      \"Setting only\",\n      \"Sentence structure\",\n      \"Theme repetition\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Dialogue, actions, and description\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Authors reveal character through what characters say, do, think, and how they're described.\",\n      \"Setting provides context but doesn't develop character.\",\n      \"Sentence structure affects style, not characterization.\",\n      \"Theme repetition reinforces meaning, not character development.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q147\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which is a recurring symbol or image that reinforces meaning?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Motif\",\n      \"Plot\",\n      \"Tone\",\n      \"Foreshadowing\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Motif\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! A motif is a repeated element that develops and reinforces the theme.\",\n      \"Plot is the sequence of events, not a recurring symbol.\",\n      \"Tone is the author's attitude, not a recurring element.\",\n      \"Foreshadowing hints at future events but isn't necessarily recurring.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q148\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Tone reveals the author's…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Mood\",\n      \"Attitude\",\n      \"Characterization\",\n      \"Diction\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Attitude\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Mood is the emotional atmosphere for readers, not the author's attitude.\",\n      \"Correct! Tone expresses the author's attitude toward the subject and audience.\",\n      \"Characterization develops characters, not tone.\",\n      \"Diction (word choice) creates tone but isn't what tone reveals.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q149\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Mood affects the…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Reader's emotions\",\n      \"Author's perspective\",\n      \"Character's motivation\",\n      \"Sentence rhythm\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Reader's emotions\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Mood creates the emotional atmosphere that influences how readers feel.\",\n      \"Author's perspective relates to tone, not mood.\",\n      \"Character motivation drives plot, not mood.\",\n      \"Rhythm is a stylistic element, distinct from mood.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q150\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Imagery appeals to…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Grammar rules\",\n      \"The five senses\",\n      \"Symbolism\",\n      \"Syntax\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"The five senses\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Grammar provides structure, not sensory experience.\",\n      \"Correct! Imagery uses descriptive language that engages sight, sound, touch, taste, and smell.\",\n      \"Symbolism uses objects for meaning; imagery creates sensory experience.\",\n      \"Syntax is sentence structure, not sensory description.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q151\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Hard\",\n    \"question\": \"An allegory contains…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Only figurative language\",\n      \"Both literal and symbolic meanings\",\n      \"One simple theme\",\n      \"Historical facts only\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Both literal and symbolic meanings\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Allegory uses multiple literary devices, not just figurative language.\",\n      \"Correct! Allegory works on two levels: the surface story and its deeper symbolic meaning.\",\n      \"Allegories often explore complex, multi-layered themes.\",\n      \"While some allegories reference history, they're primarily symbolic narratives.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q152\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Foreshadowing helps to…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Create suspense and anticipation\",\n      \"Summarize past events\",\n      \"Reveal the moral\",\n      \"Confuse readers intentionally\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Create suspense and anticipation\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Foreshadowing plants clues that build anticipation for future events.\",\n      \"Summarizing past events is exposition or flashback, not foreshadowing.\",\n      \"Revealing morals is the function of theme or resolution.\",\n      \"Good foreshadowing enhances understanding, not confusion.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q153\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Conflict in literature functions to…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Stall character development\",\n      \"Create action and reveal growth\",\n      \"Describe setting\",\n      \"Provide exposition\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Create action and reveal growth\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Conflict drives development, not stalls it.\",\n      \"Correct! Conflict generates plot tension and forces characters to change and grow.\",\n      \"Setting description is separate from conflict's function.\",\n      \"Exposition provides background; conflict creates tension.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q154\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Diction influences…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The story's rhyme\",\n      \"Tone and meaning\",\n      \"Theme repetition\",\n      \"Sentence count\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Tone and meaning\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Rhyme relates to sound patterns in poetry, not diction's primary function.\",\n      \"Correct! Word choice (diction) shapes both the tone and the precise meaning of the text.\",\n      \"Motif creates repetition, not diction itself.\",\n      \"Sentence count is unrelated to word choice.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q155\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which is an example of verbal irony?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The opposite of what's said is meant\",\n      \"A surprise ending\",\n      \"Repetition of vowel sounds\",\n      \"A symbol representing an idea\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"The opposite of what's said is meant\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Verbal irony occurs when someone says the opposite of what they actually mean (like sarcasm).\",\n      \"A surprise ending may involve situational irony, not verbal.\",\n      \"Repetition of vowel sounds is assonance, a sound device.\",\n      \"This describes symbolism, not irony.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q156\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Symbolism helps readers…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Understand literal events only\",\n      \"Find deeper meaning in concrete details\",\n      \"Track dialogue\",\n      \"Identify tone shifts\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Find deeper meaning in concrete details\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Symbolism adds layers beyond literal meaning.\",\n      \"Correct! Symbols use concrete objects to represent abstract ideas and deeper themes.\",\n      \"Dialogue tracking is a separate reading skill.\",\n      \"Tone shifts are identified through diction and style changes.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q157\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Plot is best defined as…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The message of the story\",\n      \"The sequence of related events\",\n      \"The setting's location\",\n      \"The author's word choice\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"The sequence of related events\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"The message is theme, not plot.\",\n      \"Correct! Plot is the connected series of events that make up the narrative.\",\n      \"Location is an element of setting.\",\n      \"Word choice is diction.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q158\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"The climax of a story is…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The turning point or moment of greatest tension\",\n      \"The introduction\",\n      \"The falling action\",\n      \"The resolution\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"The turning point or moment of greatest tension\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! The climax is the story's peak moment where the main conflict reaches its highest intensity.\",\n      \"The introduction is the exposition, beginning the story.\",\n      \"Falling action follows the climax, leading to resolution.\",\n      \"Resolution concludes the story after the climax.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q159\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which is an example of formative assessment?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Final exam\",\n      \"Weekly quiz\",\n      \"Report card grade\",\n      \"Standardized test\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Weekly quiz\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Final exams are summative, measuring achievement at the end.\",\n      \"Correct! Weekly quizzes provide ongoing feedback to guide instruction during the learning process.\",\n      \"Report cards are summative evaluations.\",\n      \"Standardized tests are summative measures of overall achievement.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q160\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Scaffolding helps students by…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Increasing independent learning through gradual support removal\",\n      \"Assigning more homework\",\n      \"Memorizing vocabulary lists\",\n      \"Focusing on spelling drills only\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Increasing independent learning through gradual support removal\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Scaffolding provides temporary support that's gradually withdrawn as students gain competence.\",\n      \"More homework doesn't necessarily provide structured support.\",\n      \"Memorization is one strategy, not scaffolding.\",\n      \"Spelling drills are specific practice, not the scaffolding concept.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q161\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"A rubric ensures…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Subjective grading\",\n      \"Consistent and transparent evaluation\",\n      \"Faster essay grading only\",\n      \"Less teacher involvement\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Consistent and transparent evaluation\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Rubrics reduce subjectivity by providing clear criteria.\",\n      \"Correct! Rubrics define expectations and standards, ensuring fair and consistent assessment.\",\n      \"While rubrics may speed grading, their main purpose is consistency and clarity.\",\n      \"Rubrics require thoughtful teacher design and application.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q162\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Fluency in reading includes…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Memorizing text\",\n      \"Reading with accuracy, speed, and expression\",\n      \"Quiet reading only\",\n      \"Summarizing content\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Reading with accuracy, speed, and expression\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Fluency involves decoding, not memorization.\",\n      \"Correct! Fluent readers demonstrate accuracy, appropriate rate, and prosody (expression).\",\n      \"Fluency applies to both oral and silent reading.\",\n      \"Summarizing demonstrates comprehension, not fluency.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q163\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which stage comes first in the writing process?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Revising\",\n      \"Editing\",\n      \"Prewriting\",\n      \"Publishing\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Prewriting\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Revising comes after drafting.\",\n      \"Editing comes near the end of the process.\",\n      \"Correct! Prewriting includes brainstorming, planning, and organizing ideas before drafting.\",\n      \"Publishing is the final stage.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q164\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Hard\",\n    \"question\": \"Metacognition involves…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Word memorization\",\n      \"Monitoring one's own understanding and strategy use\",\n      \"Copying notes\",\n      \"Listening silently\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Monitoring one's own understanding and strategy use\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Memorization is a learning strategy, not metacognition.\",\n      \"Correct! Metacognition is awareness and regulation of one's own thinking processes.\",\n      \"Copying is a mechanical task without reflective thinking.\",\n      \"Passive listening doesn't involve metacognitive awareness.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q165\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"The goal of peer review is to…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Grade peers\",\n      \"Provide constructive feedback to improve writing\",\n      \"Eliminate grammar errors only\",\n      \"Replace teacher feedback\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Provide constructive feedback to improve writing\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Peers provide feedback, not grades.\",\n      \"Correct! Peer review helps writers improve through constructive, specific feedback from classmates.\",\n      \"While grammar matters, peer review addresses all aspects of writing.\",\n      \"Peer review complements, not replaces, teacher feedback.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q166\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Differentiated instruction means…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Teaching everyone the same way\",\n      \"Tailorin