culties, not aids learning.\",\n      \"Interlanguage is the learner's evolving system, not the transfer itself.\",\n      \"Code-switching alternates languages, not transfer of patterns.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q208\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"The transitional system combining elements of L1 and L2 is called:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Code-switching\",\n      \"Interlanguage\",\n      \"Pidgin\",\n      \"Register\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Interlanguage\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Code-switching alternates between complete languages.\",\n      \"Correct! Interlanguage is the learner's evolving linguistic system between L1 and L2.\",\n      \"Pidgin is a contact language between groups, not individual learner language.\",\n      \"Register is formality level, not a developmental system.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q209\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which approach emphasizes all four language domains in lessons?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Integrative Language Teaching\",\n      \"Grammar-Translation\",\n      \"Audio-Lingual\",\n      \"Direct Method\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Integrative Language Teaching\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Integrative Language Teaching combines listening, speaking, reading, and writing in meaningful contexts.\",\n      \"Grammar-Translation focuses on written translation, not all skills.\",\n      \"Audio-Lingual emphasizes drilling and repetition, not integration.\",\n      \"Direct Method uses target language only but doesn't necessarily integrate all skills.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q210\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n    \"question\": \"Students discussing solutions collaboratively to construct meaning exhibit:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Collaborative Dialogue\",\n      \"Direct Instruction\",\n      \"Behavioral Conditioning\",\n      \"Drill and Practice\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Collaborative Dialogue\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Collaborative dialogue involves students negotiating meaning through peer interaction.\",\n      \"Direct instruction is teacher-led, not student-centered discussion.\",\n      \"Behavioral conditioning involves reinforcement, not collaborative meaning-making.\",\n      \"Drill and practice is repetitive, not collaborative or meaning-focused.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q211\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which best describes the link between language arts and other subjects?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"They are unrelated\",\n      \"Language arts reinforce cognitive skills across subjects\",\n      \"Math and science develop separately\",\n      \"Reading skills hinder science vocabulary\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Language arts reinforce cognitive skills across subjects\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Language and content are deeply interconnected.\",\n      \"Correct! Language arts skills (reading, writing, discussion) support learning across all disciplines.\",\n      \"All subjects require and develop language skills.\",\n      \"Reading skills support, not hinder, content vocabulary.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q212\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-2\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Teachers promoting 'language across the curriculum' encourage:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Grammar worksheets\",\n      \"Writing and discussion in all content areas\",\n     