ealing certainty vs. interpretation indicates bias or objectivity.\",\n      \"Syntax is sentence structure, not word choice implications.\",\n      \"Imagery creates sensory impressions, not relevant here.\",\n      \"Metaphor is figurative comparison, not relevant here.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q610\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"A consumer comparing ingredient lists and company claims practices:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Critical reading of informational texts\",\n      \"Predictive inference\",\n      \"Summative reasoning\",\n      \"Literal comprehension\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Critical reading of informational texts\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Critical reading evaluates information for accuracy, bias, and purpose—essential for consumer literacy.\",\n      \"Predictive inference anticipates outcomes, not evaluates claims.\",\n      \"Summative reasoning is synthesis, but critical evaluation is more specific.\",\n      \"Literal comprehension understands surface meaning, not evaluates critically.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q611\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"A workplace memo should be evaluated for:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Figurative language\",\n      \"Organization and accuracy\",\n      \"Rhythm and meter\",\n      \"Bias and irony\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Organization and accuracy\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Memos use literal, not figurative language.\",\n      \"Correct! Workplace documents prioritize clear organization and factual accuracy.\",\n      \"Rhythm and meter are poetic devices, not workplace writing criteria.\",\n      \"While bias awareness helps, organization and accuracy are primary.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q612\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n    \"question\": \"Recording emotional reactions to a poem in a reading journal reflects:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Critical evaluation\",\n      \"Reader response\",\n      \"Contextual decoding\",\n      \"Summarization\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Reader response\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Critical evaluation analyzes objectively; emotional reactions are subjective.\",\n      \"Correct! Reader response emphasizes personal interpretation and emotional engagement.\",\n      \"Contextual decoding determines word meanings, not emotional reactions.\",\n      \"Summarization condenses content, not records reactions.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q613\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Writing across content areas enhances learning because it:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Reduces comprehension load\",\n      \"Forces rote memorization\",\n      \"Deepens understanding through reflection\",\n      \"Eliminates the need for reading\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Deepens understanding through reflection\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Writing increases cognitive engagement, not reduces it.\",\n      \"Writing to learn encourages reflection, not memorization.\",\n      \"Correct! Writing clarifies thinking, connects ideas, and deepens conceptual understanding.\",\n      \"Writing complements reading, not replaces it.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q614\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n    \"question\": \"A diagram illustrating relationships between ideas supports which communication mode?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Visual\",\n      \"Auditory\",\n      \"Kinesthetic\",\n      \"Narrative\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Visual\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Diagrams are visual representations showing relationships spatially.\",\n      \"Auditory involves sound, not diagrams.\",\n      \"Kinesthetic involves movement/touch, not visual diagrams.\",\n      \"Narrative tells stories sequentially, not spatial relationships.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q615\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"An advertisement saying 'Everyone is switching to this phone!' demonstrates:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Testimonial\",\n      \"Bandwagon\",\n      \"Card-stacking\",\n      \"Transfer\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Bandwagon\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Testimonial uses individual endorsements, not claims about 'everyone.'\",\n      \"Correct! Bandwagon suggests joining the crowd—everyone's doing it, so should you.\",\n      \"Card-stacking presents only positive information, different technique.\",\n      \"Transfer associates product with positive symbols, not crowd appeal.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q616\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Selecting a graphic organizer for comparing two concepts represents:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Visual literacy\",\n      \"Propaganda analysis\",\n      \"Bias detection\",\n      \"Phonemic awareness\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Visual literacy\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Visual literacy includes creating and interpreting visual representations like graphic organizers.\",\n      \"Propaganda analysis evaluates persuasive techniques, not organizer selection.\",\n      \"Bias detection identifies favoritism, not relevant here.\",\n      \"Phonemic awareness involves sound manipulation, not visual organization.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q617\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"A documentary using both interviews and background music to persuade demonstrates:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Synergy in media\",\n      \"Ethos appeal\",\n      \"Negative bias\",\n      \"Descriptive narrative\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Synergy in media\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Synergy occurs when multiple media elements (audio + visual) work together for combined effect.\",\n      \"Ethos is credibility appeal, not multimodal integration.\",\n      \"Music choice might indicate bias, but synergy describes the integration.\",\n      \"Descriptive narrative tells details, not combines media modes.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q618\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Evaluating whether an online article is objective involves checking:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Hyperlinks\",\n      \"Author credentials and tone\",\n      \"Font style\",\n      \"Sentence length\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Author credentials and tone\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Hyperlinks indicate sources but don't determine objectivity alone.\",\n      \"Correct! Author expertise and neutral tone are key indicators of objectivity.\",\n      \"Font style is aesthetic, not related to objectivity.\",\n      \"Sentence length affects readability, not objectivity.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q619\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Which activity best builds metacognitive reading awareness?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Timed silent reading\",\n      \"Think-aloud modeling\",\n      \"Multiple-choice quizzes\",\n      \"Copying vocabulary\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Think-aloud modeling\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Silent reading doesn't explicitly demonstrate thinking processes.\",\n      \"Correct! Think-aloud modeling makes metacognitive strategies (monitoring, questioning, clarifying) visible and explicit.\",\n      \"Quizzes assess comprehension but don't build metacognitive awareness.\",\n      \"Copying vocabulary is rote practice, not metacognitive.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q620\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Comparing multiple interpretations of the same poem teaches students to:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Discredit authorial intent\",\n      \"Appreciate diversity of meaning\",\n      \"Memorize definitions\",\n      \"Focus on grammar\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Appreciate diversity of meaning\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Multiple interpretations complement, not discredit, authorial intent.\",\n      \"Correct! Diverse interpretations validate reader response and show that meaning is constructed, not singular.\",\n      \"Comparing interpretations involves analysis, not memorization.\",\n      \"Grammar is not the focus of interpretation comparison.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q621\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"A student writing reflective journal entries about lab experiments is:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Practicing writing to learn\",\n      \"Summarizing literature\",\n      \"Composing persuasive essays\",\n      \"Practicing syntax drills\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Practicing writing to learn\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Writing to learn uses informal writing to process and reflect on content learning.\",\n      \"This is science content, not literature.\",\n      \"Reflective journals are exploratory, not persuasive.\",\n      \"Syntax drills are grammar exercises, not reflection.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q622\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Analyzing how a chart supports textual information demonstrates:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Visual interpretation\",\n      \"Metaphorical reading\",\n      \"Syntax comprehension\",\n      \"Summative reasoning\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Visual interpretation\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Visual interpretation extracts meaning from visual data representations like charts.\",\n      \"Metaphorical reading interprets figurative language, not charts.\",\n      \"Syntax comprehension analyzes sentence structure, not visual data.\",\n      \"Summative reasoning synthesizes ideas but isn't specific to visual data.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q623\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"When evaluating a website, which criterion is LEAST useful?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Design aesthetics\",\n      \"Author's credentials\",\n      \"Date of publication\",\n      \"Evidence citations\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Design aesthetics\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! While design matters for usability, aesthetics don't determine credibility or accuracy.\",\n      \"Author credentials indicate expertise and credibility—essential.\",\n      \"Publication date shows currency—important for time-sensitive topics.\",\n      \"Evidence citations demonstrate research quality—essential.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q624\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n    \"question\": \"The purpose of a public service announcement is primarily to:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Entertain\",\n      \"Inform or persuade\",\n      \"Amuse\",\n      \"Narrate\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Inform or persuade\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"PSAs can engage but entertainment isn't the primary purpose.\",\n      \"Correct! PSAs inform audiences about issues and/or persuade them toward action or behavior change.\",\n      \"Amusement may be a technique but not the goal.\",\n      \"Narration is a method, not a purpose.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q625\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"A speaker using celebrity endorsements to influence an audience uses which propaganda technique?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Transfer\",\n      \"Testimonial\",\n      \"Plain folks\",\n      \"Fear appeal\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Testimonial\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Transfer associates with symbols/concepts, not specific endorsers.\",\n      \"Correct! Testimonial uses endorsements from individuals (especially celebrities) to build credibility.\",\n      \"Plain folks presents speaker as ordinary person, opposite of celebrity.\",\n      \"Fear appeal uses threats or warnings, not endorsements.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q626\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Recognizing that film uses close-up shots to create empathy demonstrates:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Critical media analysis\",\n      \"Visual confusion\",\n      \"Phonemic awareness\",\n      \"Literal comprehension\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Critical media analysis\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Critical media analysis examines how technical choices (like shot selection) shape meaning and emotion.\",\n      \"This shows understanding, not confusion.\",\n      \"Phonemic awareness involves sound manipulation, not film analysis.\",\n      \"Literal comprehension understands surface meaning, not analyzes technique.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q627\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-4\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Identifying how background music intensifies a news segment's emotional tone analyzes:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Nonverbal cues in media\",\n      \"Logical appeals\",\n      \"Morphological structure\",\n      \"Syntax\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Nonverbal cues in media\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Nonverbal cues in media include music, sound effects, and visuals that shape emotional response.\",\n      \"Logical appeals use reasoning, not music.\",\n      \"Morphological structure relates to word formation, not media.\",\n      \"Syntax is sentence structure, not media production.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q628\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"A middle school teacher has students read excerpts from a famous speech before writing their own persuasive paragraphs on a modern topic. To strengthen the connection between reading and writing, the teacher asks students to analyze the rhetorical techniques used in the speech before they draft their own work. The primary benefit of this activity is that it helps students:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"memorize formal patterns of written and spoken argument.\",\n      \"transfer comprehension strategies from reading into composition.\",\n      \"imitate the stylistic conventions of historical texts.\",\n      \"focus on correct spelling and punctuation while writing.\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"transfer comprehension strategies from reading into composition.\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Memorization is not the focus; understanding and application of rhetorical techniques is the goal.\",\n      \"Correct! Students are connecting analytical reading (how rhetoric works) with their own writing decisions—an integrated literacy practice.\",\n      \"Imitation is not the main goal; transferring analytical skills to composition is the focus.\",\n      \"Spelling and punctuation are not the primary focus of analyzing rhetorical techniques.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q629\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"After studying short stories with strong character development, students are asked to perform short dramatic readings of key scenes before writing a reflective essay about character motivation. The main advantage of this sequence is that it enables students to:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"compare film and literature as forms of storytelling.\",\n      \"understand narrative pacing through silent reading.\",\n      \"internalize literary characterization through expressive performance.\",\n      \"demonstrate memorization skills for key literary passages.\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"internalize literary characterization through expressive performance.\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Film comparison is not part of this activity; the focus is on dramatic reading and writing.\",\n      \"Silent reading is not the method used here; students are performing aloud.\",\n      \"Correct! Oral interpretation deepens comprehension and helps students feel how language shapes character and tone.\",\n      \"Memorization is not the goal; understanding character motivation through performance is the focus.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q630\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"A teacher plays an audio recording of a contemporary poet reading their own work, then asks students to analyze how the poet's vocal delivery affects meaning. Students then record themselves reading one of their own poems aloud. This assignment primarily promotes students' ability to:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"evaluate how spoken language choices convey nuance and emotion.\",\n      \"identify phonemic awareness in a literary context.\",\n      \"assess the poet's adherence to standard pronunciation norms.\",\n      \"memorize and recite poetry for performance competition.\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"evaluate how spoken language choices convey nuance and emotion.\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! It links listening and speaking to interpretation—core ELA integration.\",\n      \"Phonemic awareness relates to sound manipulation in language learning, not poetry analysis.\",\n      \"Standard pronunciation is not the focus; vocal delivery and meaning are the goals.\",\n      \"Memorization and competition are not the objectives; analysis and self-expression are the focus.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q631\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"Students in an English class maintain a weekly blog where they respond to class readings and comment on one another's posts. This activity most directly supports development in which area?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"grammar and sentence mechanics\",\n      \"collaborative writing and audience awareness\",\n      \"historical literary analysis\",\n      \"memorization of key vocabulary terms\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"collaborative writing and audience awareness\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"While grammar may be practiced, it is not the primary focus of blogging and commenting.\",\n      \"Correct! Commenting and responding online merges reading, writing, and communication skills while reinforcing authentic audience awareness.\",\n      \"Historical literary analysis may occur but is not the main benefit of the blog activity.\",\n      \"Memorization is not a focus; the activity emphasizes interaction and communication.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"Q632\",\n    \"type\": \"mcq\",\n    \"mode\": \"Drill\",\n    \"subareaId\": \"SA-1\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\n    \"question\": \"An English teacher asks students to create short podcasts explaining the themes of assigned novels and to include brief quotations to support their points. This approach best fosters:\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"oral fluency through repeated reading practice.\",\n      \"integrated comprehension by synthesizing speaking, reading, and writing skills.\",\n      \"technical editing of recorded audio files.\",\n      \"memorization of literary quotations for assessment purposes.\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"integrated comprehension by synthesizing speaking, reading, and writing skills.\",\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Oral fluency may improve, but the main goal is integrating multiple literacy skills.\",\n      \"Correct! Students read to gather evidence, write to plan their script, and speak to communicate analysis—pure language arts integration.\",\n      \"Technical editing is a side skill, not the primary educational focus.\",\n      \"Memorization is not the goal; synthesis and communication of ideas are the focus.\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1\n  }\n]\n;\n});","lineCount":4559,"map":[[4559,3]],"functionMap":null},"type":"js/module"}]}